{
  "$comment": "Shared contrast contract. Consumers: tools/check-contrast.mjs (build gate), the PHP save-time validator (P1), and the panel's advisory readout (P2). Adding a rule here must not require editing any consumer. A rule carrying \"themeAware\": true (the --bl-content-*/status-on-content-bg rules near the end of the list) is checked TWICE by check-contrast.mjs: once here against style.css's plain :root (the light palette, exactly like every other rule), and again in a separate dark-mode pass against style.css's :root[data-theme=\"dark\"] block -- design spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-22-blueline-theme-toggle-design.md §3/§7. A rule with no such flag is chrome or a fixed button/accent pairing whose value never changes between the two palettes, so re-checking it against the dark block would only repeat the same light-mode number under a misleading label.",
  "version": 1,
  "thresholds": {
    "$comment": "The declared AA floor, read verbatim by inc/team-colors.php's blueline_contrast_threshold(). This used to be INFERRED from rules[].min (body = max of all mins, large = min of all mins) -- a heuristic over data that any future rule could silently move. Adding an AAA-strength rule with \"min\": 7.0 below would have raised 'body' to 7.0 for every team-colour computation on the site with no change anywhere near team-colors.php. Declaring the floor here instead means rules can carry any min/max they need without ever affecting what \"AA\" means elsewhere.",
    "body": 4.5,
    "large": 3.0
  },
  "rules": [
